{"name":"Advent Purple","hex":"#4b365f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"advent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Arrival; onset; a time when something first comes or appears; the time when it is approaching."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To arrive or begin, especially at the first coming or appearance of something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advent"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Advent","blocks":[{"text":"Advent is a season observed in most Christian denominations as a time of waiting and preparation for both the celebration of Jesus's birth at Christmas and Jesus's return at the Second Coming. It begins on the fourth Sunday before Christmas, often referred to as Advent Sunday. Advent is the beginning of the liturgical year in Western Christianity. The name comes from Latin adventus, translating the Greek parousia from the New Testament, originally referring to the Second Coming."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Advent2007candlelight.JPG/330px-Advent2007candlelight.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advent","wikidata":"Q83012"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/Saint_Perpetuus_from_Tours.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/Saint_Perpetuus_from_Tours.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A representation of Saint Perpetuus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaint_Perpetuus_from_Tours.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Katedr%C3%A1la_sv._V%C3%ADta_ror%C3%A1ty.jpg/500px-Katedr%C3%A1la_sv._V%C3%ADta_ror%C3%A1ty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Katedr%C3%A1la_sv._V%C3%ADta_ror%C3%A1ty.jpg/1280px-Katedr%C3%A1la_sv._V%C3%ADta_ror%C3%A1ty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Katedr%C3%A1la_sv._V%C3%ADta_ror%C3%A1ty.jpg/500px-Katedr%C3%A1la_sv._V%C3%ADta_ror%C3%A1ty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rorate Mass in Prague Cathedral, Czech Republic","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKatedr%C3%A1la_sv._V%C3%ADta_ror%C3%A1ty.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/A